GooseCraft 0.11.1: graphical scene and seeded terrain prototype
usage: goosecraft-client [--world FILE | --no-save] [--preview | --replay | --seam-replay]
       [--offscreen] [--empty] [--frames N] [--screenshot FILE]
       [--seed 0..4294967295 | --demo-world] [--terrain-replay]
       [--radius 1..4] (new regular games default to 4: 81 chunks, 144x144)
       [--profile NEW-FILE.json [--profile-warmup N]]
       [--mesh-radius 0..4] (regular games default to 2; 0 keeps the whole world)
       --paged-world DIR enables bounded CPU paging; mesh-radius must be 1 or 2. Existing GCW files stay separate.
Paged diagnostics require new .png screenshot files and .json profile files.
Paged preparation uses one Goose worker; --sync-paging selects the synchronous baseline.
Diagnostics: --prefetch-delay-ms 0..100 delays the worker; --page-delay-ms 0..20 delays each page preparation.
Diagnostics: --paging-replay walks farther before returning; default 680 frames.
Diagnostics: --retain-meshes keeps all GPU meshes but draws the same mesh-radius window; --stream-replay walks out and respawns.
WASD move; mouse/arrows look; Space jump; LMB break; RMB place; 1/2 block.
Escape pauses; click/Enter resumes; R respawns; F5 saves; F10 quits and saves.
Default world: user profile / GooseCraft/worlds/default-v1.gcw. Player position is not saved.
New worlds: terrain v1, seed 12345. --seed applies only to a new world; existing saves are preserved.
Diagnostics: --single-chunk; --reference-renderer; --view-away (preview only); --seam-replay requires --demo-world.
Diagnostics: --raw-greedy disables edge stitching; --preview-view 0..3 changes overview direction.
Replay, preview and single-chunk modes are temporary unless --world is explicit.
Preview/replay/demo default to radius 1. Existing saves keep their size; --radius must match when reopening.
Diagnostics: --far-replay starts at x=31.5 to cross the old boundary; requires radius >=2.
Profile: wall-clock CPU loop samples, last 1024 after 30 warmup frames; exported on clean exit. Use a new path.
